>I have a TK50 tape drive, but no documentation.  Would someone please tell me
>what the capacity of a TK50 tape is?

95+/- MB.  The exact capacity will depend upon who you talk to, but 95MB is
a middle-of-the-road answer.

>
>We have a TK70 tape drive on a different system, and I understand it's capacity
>is 298 Mb.  Is that correct?
+/-.  I have heard 295MB and 296MB, so 28 is just as good an answer.

>
>We received a TK70 tape with software on it, which we read on the system with
>the TK70 drive.  We want to re-use the tape on the TK70 drive, but it was
>apparently written on a TK50 tape drive, and the TK70 drive won't let us write
>on the tape.  Is there something I can do to "re-format" the tape, so it can be
>used on the TK70 drive?

I assume you mean that you have a CompacTape II which has been initialized to
TK50 format by whoever supplied you the software.  If that is the case, you
might try just initializing the tape in your TK70 drive.  If that doesn't work,
try getting one of those really high-powered deguasing electromagnets and use
it to zap any existing format before trying to initialize the tape.  If you
have any type of internal security organization which erases disks/tapes
they may be able to help you.
