Nelson,

  Carpal Tunnel Syndrome is NO FUN. If you are indeed hurting, please go see
a doctor soon. One of my friends has been out for months with inflamed wrists.
It may be the keyboard, your office set up, the chair, how you hold things. I
saw a little presentation on it here by the health folks and it's a non-trivial
issue.


  There are a couple of companies that make other keyboards for DEC machines.
A number of them for "industrialized" versions. You'll have to check the trade
rags for one as that's not an item we currently carry in the TRI/ADD Catalog.

  There are more possibilities in the offing with the ACCESS.bus interface
that exists on the new Personal DECstation 5000/2x machines. The current
software doesn't provide full support (it's actually SERIAL.bus, for now) but
the idea is to let anybody eventually build any keyboard, mouse, etc., devices
for ACCESS.bus which would give you what you are looking for. 

  In the near-term though, you'll have to go for one of the current third party
folks. Sorry.

