I use the following .xmodmaprc file, use by putting the following
line in .X11Startup:

xmodmap .xmodmaprc

The .xmodmaprc file does the following:

  switches the control and caps lock keys (caps lock is now control)

  puts escape where ~/` is

  puts </> over ,/. (where they belong!)

  puts ~/' where </> used to be (next to the left shift key)

These maps for for all the X clients I've tried (xterm, emacs, etc).

It is kinda entertaining to watch someone try to type on my system when
the key legends don't match what the key does.  :-)


