I received and installed the patch for nfs_server.{c,o} which changes
NFS write from being synchronous to asynchronous.  All I can say is:

                       - + *  W O W  * + -

I put it up on one of our NFS servers and NFS write performance is
now ~7.5 times faster.  Before someone else points it out:

        * This ain't supported, no how, no way.
        * It violates the NFS spec (big deal).
        * A machine crash *can* cause you to loose the last few
          seconds worth of writes (same as with local disks).

But, since our servers are solid and have UPS+generator backup,
(in fact the last time many of them were down was to wire into the UPS),
I think our risk/benefit picture is pretty clear.


Thanks again,
