Newsgroup name:
	comp.unix.bsd

Newsgroup charter:
	To be an umoderated newgroup that provides a forum for
	discussion of BSD-derived operating systems and related topics
	including new releases and upgrade issues.

Newsgroup justification:
	An increase in interest in BSD Unix in 5 or so newgroups that
	aren't really intended to cater for this discussion has
	occurred, due to the impending release of BSD4.4, BSDI's
	BSD/386, and CMU's BSD4.4 server for Mach, in addition to the
	GNU HURD.  With the existing installed base of BSD systems, it
	is likely that comp.unix.bsd will become a viable newsgroup.
	If further specialisation is required at a future date, new
	groups can be created as part of a hierarchy.

This newsgroup received 370 YES votes, and 27 NO votes during the voting
period (13 Jan 1992 to 23:59 12 Feb 1992).  As the excess of YES votes
over NO votes was more than 100, and 2/3 of the votes were YES, this
newsgroup should be created.

