I can't say anything about async on the VLC, but I can say that thin Ethernet
only is a BAD choice. DEC tried that on the 2000 and got beaten up about it big
time. They had to quickly reengineer the box to add an AUI connector.

If you have an AUI connector, you can just plug in a transceiver for whetever
media you have. We have 10baseT. Equipment with only a BNC requires a 10baseT
to 10base2 converter at several hundred dollars. a tranceiver for 10baseT is
under $100. And it's trivial to switch over to 10base2 or 10base5 if the
equipment moves.

