Just to expand on the subject, we went through the same decisions on the ports
for the DECstations. We had a lot of trouble with customers who had Thickwire
installations and didn't like having to use DESPRs or DEMPRs to conect up the
DS5000/200 systems. We also didn't have room to do a switchable version like
we had on the DS2100/DS3100 because in order to pass PTT certification for
Europe we had to get rid of the MMJ type connectors on the serial ports and go
to 25 pin D-sub connectors.

We went to Thickwire on the DS5000/1xx and DS5000/xx systems because it only
requires a DESTA (or one of the knock-offs like Milan, which by the way can
be mounted directly to the DECstation system box while the DESTA requires a
tranceiver cable) which is a fraction of the cost of a DESPR or DEMPR.

There is a lot of system I/O on these machines these days. Just looking across
the back of a Personal DECstation 5000/xx you'll find:

SCSI	Ethernet	ISDN	Audio	ACCESS.bus	Serial 	Video


Trying to add much more than that would mean it couldn't be rack-mounted. This
isn't an excuse, just and explanation of why.

				Thanx,
				  AJ


