I think you're probably wasting your time. I've never seen a PostScript printer
that was fast enough to keep up with a 9600 bps line, let alone 19.2K, on
complex graphics. Slow printing of PostScript files is generally the time it
takes the processor to generate a page from the PostScript input, not the time
to transmit the file.

