> the improvement was stunning.  I'm assuming something similar would
> happen in the DEC world.  Anybody give me a feel for how much? 

  Overall, we have not viewed the 3100s to be "..so slow" except in the 
  context that we do not have/cannot have enough memory for our needs.  That
  is, for our needs, the Achilles Heel of these machines: they have a 24 MB
  limit.  Because of that, we are upgrading them via DEC's upgrade kit, to
  5000/125s.  The latter won't give us all that much more cpu "power", but
  they have considerably greater memory capacity.




