In article <468@niktow.canisius.edu> pavlov@niktow.canisius.edu (Greg Pavlov) writes:
>In article <92045.070512DANCC@CUNYVM.BITNET>, DANCC@CUNYVM.BITNET writes:
>> A DS 3100 with 8M is not superfast.  How much improvement will be
>> noticeable to the user by going to 16M?  To 24M?  (I'm assuming these
>> increments are possible.)

The improvement will be dependant on your situation.  The memory configs
possible for ALL 3100's are as follows:
1)   8 MB (4 MB Internal + 4 MB Card)
2)   12MB (4 MB Internal + 8 MB Card)
3)   16MB (4 MB Internal + 12MB card)
3a)  16MB (4 MB internal + 8MB card + 4MB card)
4)   20MB (4 MB internal + 16MB card)
4a)  20MB (4 MB internal + 12MB card + 4 MB card)
4b)  20MB (4 MB internal + 8MB card + 8MB card)
5)   24MB (4 MB internal + 16MB card + 4MB card)
5a)  24MB (4 MB internal + 12MB card + 8MB card)
6)   28MB (4 MB internal + 16MB card + 8MB card)
6a)  28MB (4 MB internal + 12MB card + 12MB card)
7)   32MB (4 MB internal + 24MB card)
7a)  32MB (4 MB internal + 16MB card + 12MB card)

Note:
1) Only two memory cards are possible.  the stack on one another.
2) DEC does not offer the 24 MB card, nor do they offer a 12MB or 8MB
card which can be used as the first card.  They can be stacked as the
second card.
3) Clearpoint's prices are MUCH lower (about 1/3) than DEC's.
4) The 4 MB card mentioned above as the add-on, is the original supplied
with your system.  If you cant to save that investment, I would recommend
one of the configs which utilizes it as the second card.


>  In our case, we have our 3100s maxed out to their 24 MB limit and that is
                                                     ^^^^^^^^^^^
The limit is 32MB, even using DEC's hardware.
If this is indeed a VAXstation 3100, especially if it will be running
DECWindows, get as much memory as possible.  It's cheap (around $2,000 for the
24MB board), and the incrementatl costs beteen the boards is very low,
considering the price of the board to begin with.

If I have mis-read and this is not a VS3100, I appologize for the wrong info.
