  I'm not in the office (and my manuals are) but I believe the Aztec was the
name for the RC25 disk subsystem...

> Also I have one Dilog DU142 and one DEC M7454 board. They seem almost exectly
> identical to me. Are they ? Well there is a an extra dipswitch on the Dilog
> board, what is it for ?

  A Dilog DU132 is a M7454 (well actually, it's a 20M7454, but who's being
picky? 8-). The firmware is different (the DEC flavor only supports a sin-
gle drive, for example). The DU142 is a different beast,

