In article <aas.697717178@brolga> aas@brolga.cc.uq.oz.au (Alex Sergejew) writes:
>On a similer vein, how do I get a humble microVAX II (alias VS 200 I think)
>which has a qvss mono system to use the serial port on the processor board
>(ie the console port if there were no qvss) as a simple tty line with the
>qvss plugged-in and running?

You need to create a line for the "console port", /dev/ttycp.  As root, do

	cd /dev
	./MAKEDEV ttycp

and in /etc/ttys, add a line:

ttycp   "/etc/getty std.9600" vt100    on nomodem       # console tty port

Type "kill -1 1" and the line will now have a getty (login process).

	---Bob.

