Here are the replies to my "How to charge for workstation support". Thanks
to all that replied. Feel free to send me your methodology. Just to
recap, here is the original posting.


I have been given the interesting task at work to find out different
methodologies used for the charging of workstation support. So, if
you are working for a "support" organization that deals with workstations,
I would be interested in hearing from your.

NOTE: Since I do not subscribe to all the groups I am posting to, please
      respond via email. I WILL summarize to all groups (1-2 weeks).


Some thoughts:
	- Do you have general purpose workstations and/or turnkey 
	  configurations?
		- Some CAD shops may have workstations dedicated for
		  the use of a particular software package.

	- Does your organization buy all/some workstations?
		- Some support groups may only deal with the machines
		  they buy. Some areas take on "all" systems.

	- Does your organization buy all/some software?
		- Again, similar to the hardware side of things.

	- Do you monitor system "usage" (e.g. cpu, disk, io)?

	- Do you have an algorithm that you use to calculate support
	  for "new" customers?

