 to the number of hours that user worked, and charged to different 
 accounts like the user's hours; or (2) it was a 'server' type machine, 
 shared between multiple users, and a flat fee was charged, split 
 across different accounts by a decision of the manager.

 For machines not under support, an hourly rate was charged for 
 support.

>  I would also be interested in the demographics, and staff 
