  The problem is that the various (actually, by this time it's more like
"multitude") flavors of 3100 have different mounting hardware and cables.
For example, my VS3100-30 has the SCSI/SCSI controller and thus supports
14 SCSI targets. However, the looped internal cable (SCSI-A) has only 3
connectors on it. There is also a SCSI-B cable with a single connector
on it. However, the mounting plate can only handle 4 3.5" HH devices or
1 5.25" HH plus 2 3.5" HH. Various 3100's have different mounting plate
and cable combinations, some more useful than others.

> Someone please correct me if I am wrong. By the way, little gripe: Why
> is the controller hardwired to address 6 ? The 5380 which is used in
> the 3100s SCSI controller can be software-programmed for any "Own ID"
