In article <1992Jan29.213214.17079@genome.wi.edu>, joe@genome.wi.edu (Steve Lincoln) writes:
 
|> I have had an awfully hard time getting a straight and/or informed answer 
|> from DEC sales about the SZ16 "exansion box", so maybe y'all can help:
|> 
 
|> Question: What are the ergonomics of the SZ16? How may FH or HH (or a
|> combination) drives does it hold? How many with external access? What
|> is its footprint (same as BA40 or the DAT drive maybe?)  What can its
|> power supply deal with?  There is a "Half height bracket kit" on the
|> price list - what does that do?  What kind of SCSI connector does it
|> have: do I need a peculiar cable?
|> 

The SZ16 is essentially the same enclosure that is used on the VAXstation
4000 Model 60.  If you haven't seen one yet, it's about the same size as
the SZ12, however it offers additionaly capability not offered on the SZ12.

The SZ12 can hold two full-height disks, or one disk and a CD, or half-height
tape drive.  The enclosure cannot hold a disk and a TLC04 as the TLZ04 requires
a full-height opening in the front of the enclosure, and the SZ12 has only
a half-height opening.

The SZ16 has a full-height front opening, thus can hold two half-height
devices (thus, the half-height bracket kit) or a full-height device that 
requires  access for removeable devices.  It can also hold two full-height
disks with a blank panel on the front.

The SZ03 can hold a single 3=" half or third-height disk, or a floppy.

All of these enclosures use the same 50-pin CHAMP connector, thus no
special cables are necessary to use any of the expansion boxes.



|> Importantly: Are the SZ16 (and SZ03) still not qualified on
|> DECStations? (I heard that they still aren't, but they work anyway -
|> anyone know if this is still true?)
|> 
Last I knew, the DECStation folks in Palo Alto were working on the SZ03
and SZ16 for the DECstation family, however I don't know if they've 
finished the work yet. 
