|> Oddly enough, I now have the same problem with a VAX 3500 that I just
|> inherited.  If anybody knows how to get this system to use a serial
|> terminal as the console instead of the graphics display, I'd appreciate
|> a pointer.  No combination of tweaking the two switches on the KA650
|> makes any output come out on the terminal that's attached.  I did open
|> it up and set the baud rate using the rotary switch, but that made
|> no difference.
|> 
Two solutions:

First, if you want the system to behave like a MicroVAX system on power up
you'll have to remove the QVSS or QDSS graphics cards from the Q-bus.
The console ROMs on the Q-bus machines search for the graphics boards and 
will use them if they're in the bus.  If you remove the graphics boards, 
the console will then boot from a terminal and the system will behave just
as if you bought a VAXserver 3500 (ie: you have a 2 user VMS license)


Second, if you don't care if after power up, the system will search for the
graphics controller, you can then hook up your terminal and hit a few breaks 
after the system starts to boot.  That'll get the attention of the console 
program and give control (forever, until you cycle the power) to your terminal.
